From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 01:16:55 -0400
Subject: about, welcome: the version line, the Space colour swatches
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

chrome://settings/help reads "Stedding <version> · Chromium <version>
(arm64)" from a GN argument the build tooling sets from VERSION, never
"(Developer Build)" (docs/features/settings.md T10). The welcome flow's
appearance step shows the five Space colours the switcher offers and
choosing one tints the first Space at once (docs/features/welcome.md W7);
the colours move to one header both surfaces share.

Why: docs/ROUND6-PLAN.md wave 1 (R6-09, R6-10; backlog S-42, S-43).
Removable when: Chromium names the product version on its About page from a
build argument and Stedding drops the welcome flow.
